### B.4 Honest Interval

**Theorem B.13 (Honest Interval).** Under any background theory \(T\) that does not solve the hard problem, \(\Omega_T(A) \in (0,1)\).

*Proof.* The hard problem implies that no third-person measurement can conclusively establish or refute \(H_A\). Therefore \(P(H_A \mid \mathcal{C}_{\text{info}}, T)\) is neither 0 nor 1 for any finite \(\mathcal{C}_{\text{info}}\). Hence \(\Omega_T(A) \in (0,1)\). ∎

